          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} sigma-algebra
            can be interpreted as a system of possible “distinctions” that can be made in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A
            %em filtration
            on a probability space is an increasing system of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebras"} sigma-algebras
          %p
            As the intuition may suggest, it is an instantiation of the categorical notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtration
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong filtered probability space
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{A},p)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtration
            of sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebras"} sigma-algebras
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{F}_i)_{i\in I}
            where:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+set"} partially ordered set
              (often totally ordered), with finitary
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bounds"} upper bounds
            %li
              For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_i
              is a sub-sigma-algebra of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %li
              For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\le j\in I
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℱ
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msub
                        %mi ℱ
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_i\subseteq \mathcal{F}_j
          %p
            Note that a filtration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{F}_i)_{i\in I}
            as defined above is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtered object
            in the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebras"} sigma-algebras
            %span.newWikiWord
              cofiltered object
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cofiltered+object"} ?
            in the category of measurable or probability spaces. Indeed, if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}_i\subseteq \mathcal{F}_j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X
            is measurable as a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{F}_j)\to(X,\mathcal{F}_i)
